 ")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e035d3fc-5609-4b09-8363-06b07ca7a351"],

Cell["3. Which pairs are allowed", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"084a6a8b-63cc-4fa7-b570-41ce82b473fb"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:48-57 *)
   (* pairs: fields of the theory, at least one response field, each \
unordered pair once *)
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.pairFields\", AllTrue[pairs[[All, \
1]], SubsetQ[fields, #] &], Select[pairs[[All, 1]], ! SubsetQ[fields, #] &],
     \"regulator pairs must be fields of the theory\", \"pairs are fields of \
the theory\"]];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.responsePair\", \
AllTrue[pairs[[All, 1]], IntersectingQ[#, resp] &], Select[pairs[[All, 1]], ! \
IntersectingQ[#, resp] &],
     \"a regulator entry between two physical fields would break causality \
(Gamma2_{phi phi} = 0): only phibar phi and phibar phibar pairs\",
     \"only phibar-phi / phibar-phibar pairs\"]];
   pos[a_] := First[FirstPosition[fields, a]];
   pairs = (SortBy[#[[1]], pos] -> #[[2]]) & /@ pairs;
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.pairOnce\", \
DuplicateFreeQ[pairs[[All, 1]]], pairs[[All, 1]],
     \"a pair is given twice ({a, b} and {b, a} are the same entry: R is \
symmetric because it is even in q and w-independent)\", \"each pair given \
once\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"05b17090-d43b-4d1d-a602-5a5e8391dbd1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["SubsetQ[fields, pair]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " tests that both fields belong to the theory, and ",
 StyleBox["IntersectingQ[pair, responseFields]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " that the pair contains a response field. A ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]\[CurlyPhi]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " entry would give ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2_{",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]\[CurlyPhi]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "} ",
 StyleBox["\[NotEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 0 and break causality:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c6519b1-8452-4eda-8ebc-b3f66a89841b"],

Cell["\<\
showFailure[DefineRegulator[ansatz, {h, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" \
-> {rn}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"12d6de3d-1593-4abb-8086-53355c507cd2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each pair is then put in field order (",
 StyleBox["SortBy[#[[1]], pos]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["DeleteCases, SortBy and FirstPosition",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 02)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "): R is even in q and ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "-independent, hence symmetric, so ",
 StyleBox["{hbar, h}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["{h, hbar}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " are the same entry and may be given only once."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b19de27b-e015-453f-9509-f99be5f14b65"],

Cell["4. Your q and your k", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f3d4bfa4-7d81-4bb3-95a8-cb5f98e19805"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:59-67 *)
   (* the user writes q (loop momentum) and k (scale): any context, matched \
by name *)
   qs = symbolsNamed[pairs[[All, 2]], \"q\"]; ks = symbolsNamed[pairs[[All, \
2]], \"k\"];
   FRGAssert[\"Regulator.momentumSymbol\", Length[qs] <= 1 && Length[ks] == \
1, {qs, ks},
    \"write the entries with one loop-momentum symbol q and one scale symbol \
k, shapes as r[q^2/k^2]\"];
   kk = First[ks];
   FRGAssert[\"Regulator.scaleFree\", AllTrue[Join[ks, qs], OwnValues[#] === \
{} && DownValues[#] === {} &], Join[ks, qs], \"k and q must have no \
values\"];
   entries = Association[(#[[1]] -> If[qs === {}, #[[2]], toS[#[[2]], \
First[qs]]]) & /@ pairs];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.evenInQ\", FreeQ[Values[entries], \
Alternatives @@ qs], Select[entries, ! FreeQ[#, Alternatives @@ qs] &],
     \"R_ab must depend on q through q^2 only (even powers of q)\", \"R \
depends on q^2 only\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"3d17d770-2d6a-49be-8122-3b8461056a6c"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:25 *)
symbolsNamed[e_, name_] := Union[Cases[e, x_Symbol /; SymbolName[x] === name, \
{0, Infinity}, Heads -> True]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"df8a2f60-bf0b-4195-946b-e2fd3e5f4a59"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:27-28 *)
(* q^n -> sq^(n/2), n even: R depends on q only through q^2 *)
toS[e_, qsym_] := e /. Power[qsym, n_Integer?EvenQ] :> sq^(n/2);\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"d247f98b-1f69-4dca-b581-f492b6a2f592"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The entries are written with ",
 StyleBox["your",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " symbols ",
 StyleBox["q",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". In these lessons they live in the notebook's own context (lesson 00), in \
a script in `",
 StyleBox["Global",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" : the library cannot know in advance which symbol ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "q",
 StyleBox[" is, so ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "symbolsNamed",
 StyleBox[" finds them by their short name (",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "SymbolName",
 StyleBox[", [[Symbol and SymbolName]]). ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "k",
 StyleBox[" remains the scale symbol in every later stage, and your ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "q",
 StyleBox[" is stored as ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "\"LoopMomentum\"`."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f53e883b-05d1-4c9c-a4d0-cce114f43a0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: PatternTest",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["x_?test",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " matches x only if ",
 StyleBox["test[x]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is True; ",
 StyleBox["n_Integer?EvenQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " matches even integers.",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["toS",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " replaces ",
 StyleBox["q^n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " with n even by ",
 StyleBox["sq^(n/2)",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ": from here on, R is a function of q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " only. An odd power of ",
 StyleBox["q",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " survives the replacement, and ",
 StyleBox["Regulator.evenInQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " catches it. ",
 StyleBox["p_?test",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " differs from ",
 StyleBox["p_ /; cond",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["Patterns",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 00)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 ") only in form: the test is a function applied to the match."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"55680862-81b3-4237-bc50-4c37147caa68"],

Cell["\<\
showFailure[DefineRegulator[ansatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q/k], \"Shapes\" \
-> {rn}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"567d13ec-b2f5-49be-9ee6-8e67df432235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["sq",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is a private helper symbol standing for q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". It is the example of the shared-private-context gotcha in CLAUDE.md: \
every module's helpers live in `",
 StyleBox["FRGscalarMSR",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "Private`",
 StyleBox[" (lesson 00, section 2), so a helper called ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "sq` in another module would be the same symbol."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"402581f4-7b86-4a16-a295-e918cc249c2a"],

Cell["Context[FRGscalarMSR`Private`sq]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9cb11130-f0cf-49d2-bafb-6cbe96c9024a"],

Cell["5. What may appear in an entry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6c2f1209-da04-4a92-933e-731acc3c4726"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:69-81 *)
   allowed = Join[cps, {kk, sq}];
   bad = Complement[Cases[Values[entries], x_Symbol /; Context[x] =!= \
\"System`\", {0, Infinity}, Heads -> False], allowed];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.knownSymbols\", bad === {}, bad,
     \"R_ab may contain the couplings of the ansatz, q, k and the declared \
shapes only (in particular no frequency: R is w-independent)\",
     \"only couplings, q, k and shapes; w-independent\"]];
   bad = Complement[Cases[Values[entries], (h_Symbol /; Context[h] =!= \
\"System`\")[___] :> h, {0, Infinity}], shapes];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.onlyDeclaredShapes\", bad === {}, \
bad, \"every function in R_ab must be a declared shape\", \"the declared \
shapes are the only free functions\"]];
   bad = Cases[Values[entries], (r : Alternatives @@ shapes)[x___] /; {x} =!= \
{sq/kk^2}, {0, Infinity}];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.shapeArgument\", bad === {} && \
FreeQ[Values[entries], Derivative[__][Alternatives @@ shapes]] && \
FreeQ[Values[entries] /. (Alternatives @@ shapes)[sq/kk^2] -> 1, Alternatives \
@@ shapes],
     bad, \"shapes appear only as r[q^2/k^2] (no derivatives, no other \
argument)\", \"shapes appear as r[q^2/k^2]\"]];
   used = Select[shapes, ! FreeQ[Values[entries], #] &];
   If[used =!= shapes, AppendTo[warns, infoCheck[\"WARN\", \
\"Regulator.unusedShapes\", \"declared but unused: \" <> \
ToString[Complement[shapes, used]]]]];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.nonzero\", \
AllTrue[Values[entries], # =!= 0 &], Select[entries, # === 0 &], \"drop pairs \
with R_ab = 0\", \"no zero entry\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"500be4e3-c4d4-49a5-a377-aecc596fa5b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three separate checks: only couplings, ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " and shapes as symbols (no frequency, since R is ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "-independent); only the declared shapes as functions (",
 StyleBox["(h_Symbol /; ...)[___] :> h",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " collects the heads of all function calls); and every shape only in the \
form r[q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/k",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "], with no derivative and no other argument."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6726ca8b-29e7-428d-b844-6a8544c63de4"],

Cell["\<\
showFailure[DefineRegulator[ansatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q^2/k^2] w, \
\"Shapes\" -> {rn}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"268c32f5-a36d-4003-857c-374f03c960c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Shapes stay abstract",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "The shape functions are never given a formula. The flow equations come out \
as functionals of r(y), r",
 StyleBox["\[Prime]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(y), r",
 StyleBox["\[DoublePrime]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(y), ..., valid for every regulator, and the choice (Litim, exponential, \
...) is made in FlowRG, after the export (lesson 15). Abstract shapes also \
make the symbolic checks stronger: ",
 StyleBox["ExactlyZeroQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " gives every atom r(y), r",
 StyleBox["\[Prime]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(y) its own random value (lesson 00, section 5), so an identity that passes \
holds for arbitrary shapes, not by luck for one of them. The price is that \
the shapes must appear in one fixed form, r[q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/k",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "], which is what the checks of this section enforce."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"aa703440-34c3-4652-a424-5935f17f55ec"],

Cell["6. The scale derivative, two ways", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5ad58b7b-b33d-4f13-8ca2-58e259821ac0"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:83-91 *)
   (* d_s R by the chain rule: k d/dk at fixed q; couplings c(k) -> \
dsCoupling[c] *)
   rmat = Table[Lookup[entries, Key[SortBy[{a, b}, pos]], 0], {a, fields}, \
{b, fields}];
   dsmat = Map[Expand[Sum[D[#, c] dsCoupling[c], {c, cps}] + kk D[#, kk]] &, \
rmat, {2}];
   dsAbs = Table[If[rmat[[i, j]] === 0, 0, dsR @@ SortBy[{fields[[i]], \
fields[[j]]}, pos]], {i, Length[fields]}, {j, Length[fields]}];
   (* the same derivative by a second route: couplings as functions c(k), \
total k d/dk, c'(k) -> dsCoupling[c]/k *)
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Regulator.dsRChainRule\",
     AllTrue[Flatten[dsmat - Map[(kk D[# /. Thread[cps -> (cf[#][kk] & /@ \
cps)], kk] /. Derivative[1][cf[c_]][kk] :> dsCoupling[c]/kk /. cf[c_][kk] :> \
c) &, rmat, {2}]], ExactlyZeroQ],
     dsmat, \"internal: the two computations of d_s R differ\",
     \"d_s R = sum_c dR/dc dsCoupling[c] + k dR/dk  (k d/dk r(q^2/k^2) = -2 y \
r'(y)); checked by a second route\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"500a3bc8-dbdf-4f23-8211-024933c2e753"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: D and unknown functions",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["D[e, x]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " differentiates; on a function with no definition it applies the chain rule \
and writes the derivative as ",
 StyleBox["Derivative[1][r][arg]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", displayed ",
 StyleBox["r'[arg]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ".",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["k D[rn[q^2/k^2], k]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " gives ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/k",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " r_n",
 StyleBox["\[Prime]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/k",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "), that is ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 y r",
 StyleBox["\[Prime]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(y): Mathematica knows the chain rule without knowing r. ",
 StyleBox["Derivative[1][rn]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is itself an expression, the derivative of the function ",
 StyleBox["rn",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", which is why ",
 StyleBox["ExactlyZeroQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " treats ",
 StyleBox["Derivative[1][rn][y]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " as one atom."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"6c2696ea-ce2b-4105-8670-ca818d51890e"],

Cell["k D[rn[q^2/k^2], k]", "Input",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"d2c9d288-8202-4af8-b8a8-0fef9b58d003"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Map at a level",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Map[f, matrix, {2}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " applies f to every element at depth 2, that is, to every entry of a \
matrix.",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["Map[f, {{1, 2}, {3, 4}}, {2}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["{{f[1], f[2]}, {f[3], f[4]}}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". Without the level specification, ",
 StyleBox["Map",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " would apply f to the rows."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"7d2fc755-d4eb-4ee0-8466-1e70453c1e51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first route differentiates at fixed couplings and adds ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalSigma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_c ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "R/",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "c ",
 StyleBox["\[CenterDot]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["dsCoupling[c]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". The second route makes each coupling an explicit function ",
 StyleBox["cf[c][k]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", takes the total derivative k d/dk, and replaces ",
 StyleBox["cf[c]'[k]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " by ",
 StyleBox["dsCoupling[c]/k",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["Regulator.dsRChainRule",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " requires the two to agree, with ",
 StyleBox["ExactlyZeroQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17532b9b-ea8a-46b4-9ca1-aaa850317615"],

Cell["7. The stage stores functions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"794c05c5-b07b-4eb6-aa24-3056f0f2ac75"],

Cell[BoxData[
 $CellContext`regionCells[
 "Kernel/Regulator.wl", "stage = stampStage[<", "\"Stage\" -> \"Regulator\"", 
  "\"Checks\" -> checks, \"Warnings\" -> warns"]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"9f8ad7c2-2eb2-4fa8-ac7c-2c72f9f7fb0e"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Regulator.wl:102-105 *)
RegulatorMatrix[r_Association, s_] := r[\"RMatrix\"][s];
DsRegulatorMatrix[r_Association, s_] := r[\"DsRMatrix\"][s];
DsRAbstractMatrix[r_Association] := r[\"DsRAbstract\"];
DsRRules[r_Association, s_] := \
DeleteDuplicates[DeleteCases[Flatten[MapThread[Rule, {r[\"DsRAbstract\"], \
r[\"DsRMatrix\"][s]}, 2]], 0 -> _]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"2e134696-2ffb-4278-9385-199598a7a8f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Function and Evaluate",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Function[{x}, body]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " holds its body unevaluated; ",
 StyleBox["Function[{x}, Evaluate[body]]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " evaluates it first, so the stored function contains the computed result.",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["\"RMatrix\" -> Function[Evaluate[{sq}], Evaluate[rmat]]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " stores the matrix as a function of q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["regulator[\"RMatrix\"][s]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " substitutes ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " for ",
 StyleBox["sq",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["Function",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " has the attribute ",
 StyleBox["HoldAll",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["Hold attributes",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 00)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "); without ",
 StyleBox["Evaluate",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", the body would be the ",
 StyleBox["symbol",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 StyleBox["rmat",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", a ",
 StyleBox["Module",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " variable that is gone after the call. The first ",
 StyleBox["Evaluate",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " is needed for the same reason: ",
 StyleBox["{sq}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " must be the list of the actual private symbol."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"b0783109-c295-441d-8ae2-37215e7bf1de"],

Cell["\<\
{Function[{x}, Expand[(x + 1)^2]], Function[{x}, Evaluate[Expand[(x + \
1)^2]]], regulator[\"RMatrix\"]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"e16497a5-39e4-4f71-b13c-6e931a6906e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["DsRRules",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " pairs each abstract ",
 StyleBox["dsR[a, b]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " with its derived entry (",
 StyleBox["MapThread[Rule, {m1, m2}, 2]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " builds rules entry by entry) and removes the zero entries and the \
duplicates (",
 StyleBox["DeleteDuplicates",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ": R is symmetric, so ",
 StyleBox["dsR[h, hbar]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " appears twice)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c57c8adc-cbbd-4066-bfe0-3849053a36d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Matrices as functions of q\.b2",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "The later modules need R and ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "s R at the loop momentum q, and at shifted momenta such as (q + p)",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " for the momentum projection (lesson 08). Storing a function of q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " lets each caller pass whatever it needs, ",
 StyleBox["scal[q, q]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["scal[q + p, q + p]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", without the regulator knowing about it. Since R depends on q only through \
q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " (section 4), one argument is enough."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"987faa08-4740-4b51-94d9-4b18ec297505"],

Cell["Exercises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"143e4f58-1b4e-4cde-9c90-3b44c42bc1f8"],

Cell["Exercise: \[PartialD]s R by hand", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b59f6c98-06b7-4932-8627-830a463eb7a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute k ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "k of R_{",
 StyleBox["h\:0304",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "h} = ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(k) q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " r_n(q",
